            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Welcome to the fascinating world of quantum computing! Quantum computers are not just faster versions of classical computers; they operate on fundamentally different principles, harnessing the peculiar properties of quantum mechanics to solve certain problems more efficiently.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 3,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 50
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 3,
                      "column": 278,
                      "offset": 327
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 3,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 50
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 3,
                  "column": 278,
                  "offset": 327
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "depth": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "What is OpenQASM?",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 5,
                      "column": 4,
                      "offset": 332
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 5,
                      "column": 21,
                      "offset": 349
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 5,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 329
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 5,
                  "column": 21,
                  "offset": 349
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Open Quantum Assembly Language (OpenQASM) is an intermediate representation language for quantum circuits. It allows for the description and manipulation of quantum programs, bridging the gap between high-level quantum algorithms and the low-level instructions that quantum processors execute. OpenQASM is particularly well-suited for designing experiments that test the capabilities of quantum computers with shallow (small depth) circuits.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 7,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 351
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 7,
                      "column": 442,
                      "offset": 792
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 7,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 351
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 7,
                  "column": 442,
                  "offset": 792
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Developed by researchers at IBM, OpenQASM was first introduced in a paper published on July 13, 2017, by Andrew W. Cross, Lev S. Bishop, John A. Smolin, and Jay M. Gambetta.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 9,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 794
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 9,
                      "column": 174,
                      "offset": 967
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "footnoteReference",
                  "identifier": "1",
                  "label": "1",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 9,
                      "column": 174,
                      "offset": 967
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 9,
                      "column": 178,
                      "offset": 971
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 9,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 794
